# No presumed stack (D-041)

This repository chose an ecosystem **for its own reference implementation** and recorded why:
Rust ([ADR-005](../../docs/decisions/ADR-005-reference-implementation-ecosystem.md)) and
GitHub Actions ([ADR-002](../../docs/decisions/ADR-002-host-forge-is-github.md)). Those
decisions bind this repository and nothing else.

A project cloned from this template has chosen no language, runtime, package manager, test
runner, formatter, or CI host. There is no default and no leaning, including toward the two
above.

When a stack-shaped question arises for such a project, the answer is the **constraints the
choice must satisfy**, followed by asking — not a tool named to keep moving, and not one
inferred from this repository, from the last project, or from what is popular.

Where a generic placeholder would be unreadable, a real command may be used if it is labelled
illustrative. Prefer naming the category over one instance: "the ecosystem's frozen-install
mode", "the linter's suppression escape hatch".

Reasoning and revisit trigger: [D-041](../../docs/design/10-decision-register.md).
